{"headword":"צְרוּיָה","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.pr.f.</strong> Σαρουια: mother of Abishai, Joab and Asahel;—<span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 26:6\" href=\"/I_Samuel.26.6\">1 S 26:6</a> +, <span dir=\"rtl\">צְרֻיָה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 14:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.14.1\">2 S 14:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 16:10\" href=\"/II_Samuel.16.10\">16:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:37\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.37\">23:37</a>;—according to <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:16\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.16\">1 Ch 2:16</a> a she was David’s sister; called <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵם יוֹאָב</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:25\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.25\">2 S 17:25</a>; elsewhere after cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּן־ (בְּנֵי)</span>: <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּן־צ׳</span> of Abishai <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 26:6\" href=\"/I_Samuel.26.6\">1 S 26:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 16:9\" href=\"/II_Samuel.16.9\">2 S 16:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 18:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.18.2\">18:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:22\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.22\">19:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 21:17\" href=\"/II_Samuel.21.17\">21:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 18:12\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.18.12\">1 Ch 18:12</a>; of Joab <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:13\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.13\">2 S 2:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 8:16\" href=\"/II_Samuel.8.16\">8:16</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 18:15\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.18.15\">1 Ch 18:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 14:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.14.1\">2 S 14:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.18\">23:18</a> and v <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:37\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.37\">37</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:39\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.39\">1 Ch 11:39</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 1:7\" href=\"/I_Kings.1.7\">1 K 1:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 2:5\" href=\"/I_Kings.2.5\">2:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 2:22\" href=\"/I_Kings.2.22\">22</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:6\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.6\">1 Ch 11:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 26:28\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.26.28\">26:28</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:24\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.24\">27:24</a>; pl. of all three <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.18\">2 S 2:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:16\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.16\">1 Ch 2:16</a>; Abishai and Joab <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 3:39\" href=\"/II_Samuel.3.39\">2 S 3:39</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 16:10\" href=\"/II_Samuel.16.10\">16:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:23\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.23\">19:23</a>."}]},"rid":"BDB08580","strong_numbers":["6870"],"next_hw":"צָרַח","prev_hw":"צְרִי","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["7653"],"TWOT":[],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}